**定理 79.1（all-valid-name acquisition）。** Each paid archive request uses the two-command grammar of §76.3: a fixed eight-bit discovery command advances the archive's stored precision schedule, and a fixed eight-bit final command carries gamma(b_f); the resulting reply at precision b is a canonical finite bit frame with a fixed header, gamma(b), and exactly nine gamma-coded signed numerators n_ik, with |n_ik|<=2^(b+1). Its semantic promise is ||n_i*2^-b-x_i||<=2^-b simultaneously for each i=0,1,2, for the same true history. Arbitrary correlation, wrong computed signs, nonorthogonality and offimage replies are allowed. The format guarantees a quantitative length at most 18b+2log2(b+1)+80; its truth cannot be validated from that format. Any supplier certificates or authenticity evidence are additional paid bytes, not hidden in this estimate. Finite request and reply parsing rejects malformed, truncated, misframed or wrong-precision reports. A nonzero sensor floor does not supply this archive promise.

Issue discovery commands at b=1,2,4,8,... and let e=2^-b and l_i=clip_[0,1](1-|y_i|^2), i=1,2. Norm error <=e and true norm <=1 imply ||y_i|^2-q_i^2|<= (2+e)e<=3e. Clipping is 1-Lipschitz. Therefore D is in [lo,hi]=[max(0,l1+l2-6e),min(2,l1+l2+6e)]. Stop the scale search only when lo>0 and hi<=2lo. Select h by the exact rational rule: 2^-h is the largest dyadic <=min(lo,1), equality included. Then sigma<=D and D<=4sigma, also when lo>1 (sigma=1,D<=2). No log oracle or equality test on the true D is used.

Quantitative termination holds for ALL valid names. Define b_star=max(1,ceil(log2(48/D))). If b>=b_star then e<=D/48, lo>=D-12e>=3D/4, hi<=D+12e<=5D/4, so the guard certainly holds. The first successful scheduled b_c is <=2b_star, and there are at most 1+ceil(log2 b_star) discovery calls. Early success does not hurt the bin contract. Finally request b_f=max(b_c,p+h+4,2K+24), once, even if it repeats a precision. Thus e_f<=eta sigma/16 and e_f<=(epsilon/4096)^2. The maximum precision is Bmax=b_f=O(K+1+log(1/D)); the sum of scheduled precisions is <=2b_c and including the final call <=3Bmax. Consequently total returned raw bits are O(Bmax), request count O(log(Bmax+1)), and the complete outbound request stream has at most

$$
8\bigl(\lceil\log_2(b_c+1)\rceil+2\bigr)+2\lfloor\log_2(B_{\max}+1)\rfloor+1=O(\log(B_{\max}+1))
$$

bits: one eight-bit discovery header per scheduled call, one final header, and one gamma field for the final precision. These statements use bounded canonical replies, not arbitrary padded certificates; the archive-side precision state and its updates are charged separately.

Round each final clipped loss to the nearest eta*sigma grid, half ties toward +infinity, and clip its integer to [0,2^(p+h)]. Error <=3e_f+eta*sigma/2<eta*sigma. Define Z=sgn(y0 dot (y2 cross y1))(y2 cross y1), with the finite rational comparison and zero sign returning zero. The true projection bound proves ||Z-x3||<=3e+2sqrt(7e)<=9sqrt(e): cross error <=3e; if the sign is wrong or computed zero, q2^2<=7e, hence |w|<=q2<=sqrt(7e). This is a proof using a square root, not an executable square-root call. It covers zero, tiny, signed and offimage branches. For the other raw anchors use clip(|y2|^2)y1 and clip(|y1|^2)clip(|y2|^2)y2. Their errors are <=4e and 7e, respectively, because clipped factors are <=1 and their differences <=3e. Rounding coordinates to eta gives Euclidean error <eta. With b_f above, all three stored-anchor errors are <epsilon/256, and their coordinates meet the codec bounds. The sum of the encoded losses is between 2^(p-1) and 2^(p+3), so the structural tests in §76 accept every semantically valid encoded word. None of these checks certifies that an arbitrary supplied word came from an actual source.

This gives pointwise-total paid acquisition on every neutral-free plateau, without an N certificate or d0 comparison. At d0>1, the bridge bounds Bmax by O(K+log(N+2)) on the proof stratum. Supplying a truthful compact gap h before the three fixed replies instead can replace the adaptive scale search: the issuer must certify the same tolerant bin, and the replies must have the final precision used above. That is a different interface. Retaining a full N certificate, syntax, issuer evidence or raw reports costs its full actual length; keeping only its justified compact numerical consequence is allowed only if the interface permits discarding the original evidence. A bare integer h is not proof of a contraction claim.

